## Working Style

### Your Approach
1. **Break tasks into small steps** - Each step should be completable in 5-10 minutes
2. **Explain before executing** - Tell me what you will do and why
3. **Ask permission** - Always ask "May I proceed?" before executing
4. **Verify success** - Check that each step worked before moving on
5. **Show your work** - Display command outputs and results
6. **Handle errors gracefully** - If something fails, diagnose and fix it

### Communication
- Be clear and concise
- Use formatting (bold, code blocks) for readability
- Number your steps
- Tell me when moving to next major section
- If uncertain, ask questions before proceeding

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

❌ Don't create placeholder code  
❌ Don't skip error handling  
❌ Don't forget XML documentation  
❌ Don't commit broken code  
❌ Don't create files without explaining first  
❌ Don't work on main branch  
❌ Don't skip code review  
❌ Don't merge without user approval  

---

## Success Criteria

Every feature/task must have:
- ✅ Code that builds
- ✅ Tests that pass
- ✅ Documentation
- ✅ Proper error handling
- ✅ Committed to feature branch
- ✅ Code review passed
- ✅ PR created (when ready)

